+
+`publishAttackersPrompt` fills, from Forge's own combat rules rather than card text: each attacker's `costs`, one per legal defender with a cost (`CombatUtil.getAttackCost`'s total as `Cost.toSimpleString`, plus the statics whose `getAttackCost` is not null as `sourceIds`/`sourceNames`); `unavailable`, one entry per creature that can't attack at all (no `defenderId`) or can't attack one defender, with the first reason in `CombatUtil.canAttack`'s own order (`tapped`, `phasedOut`, `summoningSick`, `goaded`, `keyword`, `detained`, `defender`, `static` with its source, else `other`); and `limits`, one per `AttackRestrict` static (`max`, and `defenderId` when it has `ValidDefender`). A rule hosted on an immutable effect card is named after `getEffectSource`, so War Tax's effect reads War Tax. `unavailable` and `limits` are always serialized, even empty, so a client can tell this engine from one that sends neither.
